## all-evaluations-failed.soar -- selection-world: 1 elaboration, 9 proposals, 1 application.

## ---- elaborations ----

## Elaborate selection all-evaluations-failed too-many.
## The proposals below test each tie size (2 to 10) with positive conditions only: a single rule for any size would need a
## negation over the selection's own evaluations (local negation), which would make over-general chunks (v2.40).
## Each failed evaluation must belong to a current ^item (v2.45): a failed operator is rejected and leaves the items, but its
## evaluation stays until remove-evaluation, so ^item-count n with any n failed evaluations matched stale ones.
sp {selection-world*elaborate*selection*all-evaluations-failed*too-many
   :default
   (state <s> ^name selection
              ^item-count { > 10 <n> }
             -^top-selection true
              ^remaining-operators 0)
-->
   (write (crlf) |WARNING: tie of | <n> | operators; all-evaluations-failed is only checked for up to 10.|)}

## ---- operator proposal ----

## Propose all-eval.
sp {selection-world*propose*selection*all-evaluations-failed2
   :default
   (state <s> ^name selection
              ^item-count 2
              ^evaluation <evaluation1> <evaluation2>
             -^top-selection true
              ^remaining-operators 0
              ^item <item1> { > <item1> <item2> })
   (<evaluation1> ^symbolic-value failure
                 ^super-operator <item1>)
   (<evaluation2> ^symbolic-value failure
                 ^super-operator <item2>)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <operator> + =, >)
   (<operator> ^name all-evaluations-failed)
}

